## Why This Question Is Asked
Evaluates the ability to design real-world, latency-constrained explainability systems that balance privacy and governance requirements in high-stakes ML environments.

## Key Concepts
- Per-instance explanations under strict latency constraints
- Privacy-preserving attribution without raw feature exposure
- Caching, bucketing, and surrogate models for performance optimization
- Drift monitoring and governance compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
function attribution(event) {
  const bucket = features.map(f => bucketize(f.value, f.schema));
  const fingerprint = hash(bucket);
  const cached = cache.get(fingerprint);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const attribution = surrogate.predict(bucket);
  cache.set(fingerprint, attribution);
  return attribution;
}
```
